From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:54:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: panorama comfortable grid flows as a staggered grid
 with wider auto columns

Two complaints about the "Panorama comfortable grid" with the column count
on auto:

- Wide covers were cramped. The auto layout used the same 128 dp minimum
  column width as the book-shaped grids, so a 3:2 cover ended up about as
  wide as a 2:3 cover and only two thirds as tall. Panorama mode now uses
  a 168 dp minimum: two columns on phones, three from ~530 dp, and a wide
  cover gets roughly the area a book cover has at 128 dp. Fixed column
  counts are unchanged.
- A 2:3 cover sharing a row with 3:2 covers left a large hole under the
  wide ones, because LazyVerticalGrid makes every row as tall as its
  tallest cell. Panorama mode now renders in a LazyVerticalStaggeredGrid,
  where each lane flows independently and cells of different heights pack
  without gaps. A fast scroller for staggered grids is added to
  presentation-core (scroll range estimated from the average visible item
  height per lane, as the irregular grid scroller does).

Cover orientation is also cached per manga for the process lifetime, so a
cell keeps its shape when it scrolls back into view instead of flipping
from book to panorama once the image decodes again; in panorama mode an
unknown cover is assumed 16:9.

Harmony-only (follow-up to 0015): Mihon has no panorama cover feature,
Animeko has no such grid.
